# Everything `regenerate.sh` produces.
#
# `nan-payloads.ct` and the ORIGINAL module the offline replay is driven
# against (spec §6.1) are NOT committed. They were, on the grounds that
# the replay runs the uninstrumented module and so needs *that* build —
# which is true, and is satisfied better by producing both in one run
# than by freezing both.
#
# It matters more here than anywhere else in the campaign that the
# recording is fresh: what the checks assert is the bit patterns the
# *browser producer* wrote (`f32:0x7f800001` and friends), so a stored
# recording would only ever confirm that some past producer agreed with
# itself. `scripts/materialize-recording.sh` keys the cache on
# `ct-instrument` and the browser recorder by content, so a change in
# either re-records.
#
# The genuine counter-example is in the sibling repo:
# `codetracer-wasm-recorder/.../nan-payloads/legacy-encoding.ct` was made
# by a `ct-instrument` built before M52 and cannot be produced from any
# current tree. That one stays committed, and must never be regenerated.
nan-payloads.ct/
module/

# Build output.
wasm-src/target/

# What the browser loads, written beside the page that serves it, built in
# the same run as the recording. The repo root's blanket `*.wasm` already
# ignores it; this is the statement of intent.
page/*.instrumented.wasm
page/*.instrumented.wasm.manifest.json
